+def reached_end(latest_stored, start, end) -> bool:
+    """A security has reached its end when NO trading day lies in (its latest stored date, the request's end].
+
+    DQ-t-34 (row MDPF_DEMQUE-Z-S3). The cell-count test it replaces could never close a request: a quote priced on
+    weekdays counts holidays the vendor never returns, so `drawn < quoted` stayed true forever and every later fire
+    appended a 0-cell DRAWN line. Trading days are the only honest cursor, because they are what the vendor returns.
+    A security with nothing stored is measured from the request's start instead, so an empty window reads reached.
